  - Modify them, or build anything derived from them, beyond changes you keep to
    yourself on your own machine.
  - Reuse their source code, in whole or in part, in any other project.
  - Present them, modified or unmodified, in whole or in part, as your own work,
    or remove or alter any credit, name or notice they carry.

The source code is published to be read, not to be reused. Publishing it grants
no licence to it of any kind, including by having seen it.

Third-party components carry their own licences and are not covered by this one.


